ent-ClothingPantsDhoti = dhoti
    .desc = A pair of baggy pants of Ranesheni origin, with a long banner-like cloth draped between the two pant legs.

ent-ClothingPantsHose = cloth hosen
    .desc = A pair of cloth leggings, traditionally worn in conjunction with one's shortclothes. These can be combined with maille hosen for the perfect blend of function-and-fashion; just pray no one has the mind to aim below the belt.

ent-ClothingPantsLeathertights = leather tights
    .desc = Classy leather tights, form-fitting but tasteful.

ent-ClothingPantsMonkpants = formal breeches
    .desc = A pair of form-fitting tights.

ent-ClothingPantsPaddedchausses = padded chausses
    .desc = A pair of cloth-armored trousers, comprised of padded hoses worn atop thickly-quilted shortclothes. Originating as an answer to labors and pilgrimages through harsher terrain, it's also been mobilized as a cost-effective means of protecting militia-legs aplenty.

ent-ClothingPantsRoguepants = hardened leather trousers
    .desc = Thick hide cut and sewn into a pair of very protective trousers. The dense leather can turn away errant chops.

ent-ClothingPantsSailorpants = sailor's pants
    .desc = A pair of form-fitting tights.

ent-ClothingPantsShalwar = shalwar pants
    .desc = A pair of cloth shalwar pants, with a baggy fit and a tapered ankle. Originating from Ranesheni, these pants are known for their comfort and ease of movement.

ent-ClothingPantsTights = tights
    .desc = A pair of form-fitting tights.

ent-ClothingPantsCloth = work trousers
    .desc = Good quality trousers worn by laborers.

ent-ClothingPantsLeather = leather trousers
    .desc = Good quality trousers worn by laborers.

ent-ClothingPantsBaggy = baggy trousers
    .desc = Loose trousers with plenty of room to move.
